        "cell": "Room for more funding!B9"
      },
      "explainer": "B2P told us that 70% of bridge building costs are paid by B2P and 30% by the government and that all maintenance costs are covered by the government. Bridge costs are about $100k, so B2P costs are about $70k. \"I’ve attached a spreadsheet (Remaining Research Bridge Budget Analysis) with an average estimated bridge cost of $104k. Maintenance is the full responsibility of the District and they budget about $400/year for maintenance... Referencing the spreadsheet above (Remaining Research Bridge Budget analysis) you’ll see on average 70% paid by B2P and 30% paid by District for the upfront build of the bridge. All maintenance costs are covered bythe District.\" Christina Barstow, Bridges to Prosperity, response to questions from GiveWell, May 3, 2022",
